ies. It also provides personal styling services through its website and mobile application. The company was formerly known as rack habit inc. and changed its name to Stitch Fix, Inc. in October 2011. Stitch Fix, Inc. was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew H. Baer | CEO & Director | Age 43 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $318K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $5K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Stitch Fix, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $359M market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -53% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $20M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 316% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.1615953562400527},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2547099.14},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Did Stitch Fix (NASDAQ:SFIX) Navigate Its Latest Fiscal Year?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/smallcap/how-did-stitch-fix-nasdaqsfix-navigate-its-latest-fiscal-year","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793747820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"